{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jc2yrwwwc6pSMBCENt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft this, I need a few answers. Investors will check the profitability claim against your numbers, and right now those numbers don't support it. At $95k a month you have about 3.5 months of cash. The $600k adds roughly 6 more months. And with 70% of your revenue landing in March–April, the next few months will be lean.\n\n1. **What's the path to profitability next year?** Give me the actual mechanics: how many beekeepers and hives you need, what monthly spend you'll get down to, and when. If you have a rough model, the key figures are enough. If there's no plan behind it yet, tell me. I'd then frame it as a target with milestones instead of a promise.\n2. **How many hives are paying the $4/month subscription today, and what's your churn?** Recurring revenue is your strongest answer both to the seasonality and to a competitor that's cheaper on hardware.\n3. **How are you responding to the $45 competitor?** Have you lost any deals or customers since May? What does your product do that theirs doesn't, like accuracy, alerts, or the app? Are you changing your pricing?\n4. **What are the bridge terms and what does it bridge to?** Is it a SAFE or a note, what's the cap or discount, how much is already committed, and is there a deadline? What milestone gets you to the next raise or to break-even?\n5. **Can I name your biggest customer and quote them?** And are you comfortable with me saying plainly that they also changed their mite treatment? I'd recommend saying it. Investors trust a result more when the update doesn't overclaim it.\n\nIf you don't know an answer, just say so and I'll write around it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":9570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_i